arked as an expected failure in the test file. I didn't run the full test suite, and I didn't run the new `docs/examples.md` doctest.\n\n- **`_compat.py`:** added `_IS_GENERATOR_RESULTS` and `_lazy_is_generator`. Unhashable hooks fall back to an uncached answer.\n- **`_make.py`:** the generated `__setattr__` now follows the spec for plain and generator hooks. It raises the `RuntimeError` if a generator yields twice. I also added the `versionchanged` note to `attrib`'s docstring.\n- **`_next_gen.py`, `setters.py`, `__init__.pyi`:** the docstring additions, the `pipe()` warning and the widened `_OnSetAttrType` are in as specified.\n- **`docs/examples.md`:** added the \"Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes\" section before `(metadata)=`.\n\nThe spec names `_ClassBuilder._make_own_setattr`, but that method doesn't exist in this checkout. The `__setattr__` generation lives in `_ClassBuilder.add_setattr`, so I changed that instead.\n\nIn the doc example, the hook prints `setting x to '67'` before yielding. The spec only said it prints the incoming value, so the exact wording is mine.", "ttft_ms": 3534, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 51199, "uuid": "3bf21cea-500c-486c-b0ab-fe104a8d53b5", "ttft_stream_ms": 2831, "time_to_request_ms": 50, "first_content_frame_ms": 2831, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
